            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography</h2>
            <p>The St Louis-to-Chicago train route runs through the heart of the Midwest, traveling north through the Illinois prairie along the Mississippi River corridor. Passengers get views of the Mississippi River, fertile farmland, small river towns, and the transition from Missouri's rolling hills to Illinois' flat prairie, making the journey more than just transit - it's a relaxed and picturesque experience.</p>
            <p>The route passes through key cities and towns such as Alton, Carlinville, Springfield, Lincoln, Normal, Pontiac, Joliet, before reaching downtown Chicago. Along the way, travelers can enjoy natural scenery, including river bluffs, cornfields, prairie landscapes, and glimpses of historic Midwest towns.</p>
