            <h2>Step-by-Step Journey Experience</h2>
            <p>Understanding the full journey from St Louis to Chicago can make your travel experience smoother and more predictable. Here's what to expect from station arrival to reaching your destination.</p>
            <h3> Arrival at the Station in St Louis</h3>
            <p>Most trains to Chicago depart from St Louis Gateway Station, conveniently located near downtown St Louis.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Recommended Arrival: </b>20-30 minutes before departure.</li>
                <li><b>Facilities:</b> Ticket counters, waiting areas, restrooms, small cafés, baggage services, paid parking, and accessible facilities.</li>
                <li><b>Architecture:</b> The modern station features contemporary design with nods to St Louis' rail heritage.</li>
                <li><b>Signage: </b>Platforms and departure boards are clearly marked for easy navigation.</li>
                <li><b>Transit Access:</b> Easily reachable via MetroLink light rail, MetroBus, and rideshare services. The Gateway Arch is within walking distance.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>  Boarding Process</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Platforms are usually announced 15-20 minutes before departure.</li>
                <li>Boarding is straightforward, with clearly marked coach and business class cars.</li>
                <li>No airport-style security checks, making the process quick and simple.</li>
                <li>Business Class passengers enjoy priority boarding.</li>
                <li>Staff are typically friendly and helpful with luggage and seating questions.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>  Onboard Experience</h3>
            <p>The St Louis → Chicago train journey is designed for comfort and relaxation:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Seating:  </b>Spacious, adjustable, with good legroom and generous recline. Coach seats offer comfort comparable to first-class airline seating.</li>
                <li><b>Amenities: </b> Overhead storage, power outlets, and free Wi-Fi (available on Lincoln Service trains).</li>
                <li><b>Environment:</b> Quiet, especially in Business Class; designated quiet cars on some services.</li>
                <li><b>Scenery:  </b>Enjoy views of the Mississippi River, Alton's river bluffs, Illinois farmland, prairie landscapes, and small Midwest towns.</li>
                <li><b>Cafe Car:  </b>Offers snacks, beverages, light meals, and alcoholic drinks during the trip.</li>
                <li><b>Accessibility: </b>Wheelchair spaces and accessible restrooms are available on the lower level of the bi-level cars.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>  Arrival in Chicago</h3>
            <p>Trains from St Louis arrive at Chicago Union Station, located in downtown Chicago's Loop, making it easy to start exploring immediately upon arrival.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Location:</b> City center, near the Loop, Millennium Park, and the Chicago River.</li>
                <li><b>Connectivity: </b>Close to CTA "L" trains (Blue, Red, Brown, Orange, Pink, Purple Lines), Metra commuter rail, buses, taxis, and rideshare pick-up zones.</li>
