                <li><b>Comfort:</b> Spacious seats, free Wi-Fi, power outlets, café car, generous legroom</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility: </b>Direct city-center to city-center service, 5 departures per day</li>
                <li><b>Pros:</b> Scenic views, no traffic stress, productive travel time, city-center arrival, comfortable seating</li>
                <li><b>Cons:</b> Longer than flight airtime, occasional delays due to freight train traffic</li>
            </ul>
            <h3> Bus</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Duration: </b>~5h 30m - 7h 00m depending on traffic and stops</li>
                <li><b>Comfort:</b> Standard coach seating; fewer amenities than train, limited legroom</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility:</b> Multiple departures per day, pick-up/drop-off at various points (Greyhound, Megabus, Burlington Trailways)</li>
                <li><b>Pros:</b> Usually cheaper than train, frequent schedules, direct city-center options</li>
                <li><b>Cons:</b> Slower in heavy traffic, less comfortable, no Wi-Fi or power outlets on all services, and multiple stops</li>
            </ul>

